    11	
    12	Members are refreshed manually with a Python command talking to the running Rust
    13	application. Rust acknowledges each committed batch before the next source page
    14	is fetched. Declarations refresh automatically in the Rust application, using a
    15	Python CLI adapter. A background task checks persisted refresh state, catches up
    16	after downtime, and retries operational failures with bounded backoff. A complete
    17	source check is due daily; failures must not advance its successful timestamp.
    18	Freshness is relative to Parliament publication, not the date of a real-world event.
    19	Daily checks also report new MPs that require a manual member refresh.
    20	
    21	Initialization reuses member refresh followed by declaration refresh. It is safe
    22	to repeat after interruption; it does not apply migrations or promise exact
    23	restoration of lost identifiers. All imports share one concurrency guard.
